-- Test Description
-- This test ensures the minimum frame size for the GEM in 10/100/1000 mode.
--
-- Functional coverage
-- � Ensures that in 10/100 mode that received frames are at least 64 bytes.
-- � Ensures that in normal 1000 mode that the minimum frame size is at least
--   64 bytes plus extension for all received frames.  Also, ensures that any
--   received frame under 512 bytes has extension added to ensure minimum 
--   slot time (512 bytes) is made.
-- � Ensures that in burst 1000 mode that the first frame in a received burst 
--   of frames is at least 64 bytes plus extension. Also, ensures that the 
--   first received frame of a burst under 512 bytes has extension added to 
--   ensure minimum slot time (512 bytes) is made.
-- � Ensures that in burst 1000 mode any frame after the first received frame 
--   of the burst is at least 64 bytes long.
--
-- Detailed Test Description
--
-- 10/100 mode minimum frame size check:
-- 1. Initialise GEM for 100-mode operation. 
-- 2. Receive an undersized frame of 40 bytes.
-- 3. Receive an undersized frame of 63 bytes.
-- 4. Receive a minimum sized frame.
-- 5. Check status registers and statistics registers and ensure that the 
--    above operations were dealt with properly.
--
-- 1000 normal mode minimum frame size check:
-- 6. Initialise GEM for 1000 mode operation.
-- 7. Receive an undersized frame of 40 bytes plus extension.
-- 8. Receive an undersized frame of 63 bytes plus extension.
-- 9. Receive a minimum sized frame plus extension.
-- 10. Receive a minimum sized frame with the incorrect amount of extension.
-- 11. Receive an undersized frame with the incorrect amount of extension.
-- 12. Receive a minimum sized frame plus extension.
-- 13. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above 
--     operations were dealt with properly.
--
-- 1000 burst mode minimum frame size check:
-- 14. In burst mode, receive an undersized frame of 40 bytes plus extension. 
--     Then, receive an undersized frame of 40 bytes.
-- 15. In burst mode, receive an undersized frame of 63 bytes plus extension.
--     Then, receive an undersized frame of 63 bytes.
-- 16. In burst mode, receive minimum sized frame plus extension. Then, receive
--     an undersized frame of 63 bytes.
-- 17. In burst mode, receive an undersized frame of 63 bytes plus extension.  
--     Then, receive a minimum sized frame.
-- 18. In burst mode, receive a minimum sized frame with the incorrect amount 
--     of extension. Then receive an undersized frame of 63 bytes.
-- 19. In burst mode, receive a minimum sized frame with the incorrect amount 
--     of extension. Then receive a minimum sized frame.
-- 20. In burst mode, receive an undersized frame of 63 bytes with the 
--     incorrect amount of extension. Then, receive a minimum sized frame.
-- 21. In burst mode, receive an undersized frame of 63 bytes with the 
--     incorrect amount of extension. Then, receive an undersized frame of 63 
--     bytes.
-- 22. In burst mode, receive a minimum sized frame with extension. Then,
--     receive a minimum sized frame.
-- 23. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above
--     operations were dealt with properly.
-- 24. In burst mode, receive a minimum sized frame with extension totalling 499 bytes (12 bytes
--     of inter-frame gap should bring the slot time up to 511 bytes. Therefore, frame 
--     should not be copied to memory). Then, receive a frame with 499 bytes of data (12 bytes
--     of inter-frame gap should bring the slot time up to 511 bytes. Therefore, frame 
--     should not be copied to memory). Then, receive a frame with 500 bytes of data.(12 bytes
--     of inter-frame gap should bring the slot time up to 512 bytes. Therefore, frame 
--     should be copied to memory). Finally,receive a minimum sized frame. 
-- 25. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above
--     operations were dealt with properly

